333 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 256 0 R
/E (REA Group operates in an increasingly competitive digital property market as artificial intelligence \(AI\) transforms property search into more conversational and personalised experiences. However, growing privacy concerns and uncertainty about AI-generated information create a challenge for REA: how can digital marketing strengthen consumer trust while increasing engagement and adoption of AI-enabled property features? )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
334 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 256 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
335 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 256 0 R
/E (Two complementary implementations are proposed. Show Your Working enhances the existing realEstimate experience through confidence ranges, visible AI disclosure, plain-English explanations of estimate calculations, a Data Control Centre and access to human review. The Estimate Explained extends this transparency into TikTok, Instagram reels and YouTube Shorts through weekly expert-led videos comparing partnerships and the #MyEstimateExplained user-generated content campaign, this initiative makes estimation outcomes more visible while encouraging audience participation. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
336 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 256 0 R
/E (The strategy establishes four six-month objectives: increase consumer trust by 15% \(Objective 1\), increase AI-feature activation by 20% \(Objective 2\), improve 30-day repeat use by 15% \(Objective 3\), and increase understanding of AI and data use by 15% \(Objective 4\). Performance will be evaluated using consumer surveys, product analytics, video engagement metrics and comprehension testing. These targets represent proposed outcomes rather than guaranteed results. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
337 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 256 0 R
/E (A proposed $1.29 million programme allocates 60% of the budget to Show Your Working, prioritising improvements to the product experience where trust concerns originate. Implementation will be supported by phased testing, privacy safeguards, verified information and transparent communication of estimation limitations.  )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
